    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0576" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1452: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow (Adams) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-21T15:00:00+08:00">February 21, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 21—4 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. My No. 27, February 9, 5 p.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d493-f1"/> Notice
                    received today from Telegraph Administration that my telegram to O’Shea was undelivered because
                    telegraph line to Kanchow destroyed by bandits. I am renewing representations to
                    Kiangsi authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Adams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
